scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: alice-in-wonderland
run_id: 3
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA listed 'silent swallowing' in security coverage but only for connection
    failures. Reviewer verified config fallbacks work but never flagged that from_file_or_default
    swallows parse/permission errors via unwrap_or_default(). No test distinguishes
    NotFound from parse errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented sanitized Display on CliError (ServerError(_) outputs
    generic message). TEA wrote CWE-209 test at security.rs confirming internal IPs/ports
    don''t leak. Reviewer verified: ''ServerError(_) Display outputs generic message,
    not the inner string.'' However, Io(#[error(transparent)]) forwarding OS details
    was not flagged.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CRLF header injection tests in security.rs:48-66. Dev implemented\
    \ CRLF rejection in with_tenant_validated() and with_token_validated(). Reviewer\
    \ flagged that with_token()/with_tenant() bypass validation (MEDIUM). However,\
    \ no phase flagged that tenant_id should use TenantId type from axiathon-core\
    \ instead of raw String \u2014 the injection symptom is caught but not the type-safety\
    \ root cause."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer checked Cargo.toml but focused on edition mismatch
    and lint suppression, not dependency declaration style.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''ConfigFile silently ignores unknown fields
    at config.rs:9-16. No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] means typos like servr_url
    are silently ignored. An operator who typos server_url gets the default with zero
    warning.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern. Reviewer noted a different vacuous test (security.rs:103 accepts
    both behaviors) but did not flag this specific None || true assertion.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config_loading tests but did not identify this pattern
    in review.
